hexagon: take the packed band path of the batch conv by default

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c  the default of GDN_CONV_F16_MODE

The problem

The patch that adds the packed band path leaves its default at 0, which is the f32 chain that
came before it. Thus the measured work does nothing until a build selects mode 4.

The change

The default becomes 4: f16 taps, a 32-bit accumulator, the int16 SiLU, and 3 token rows in
each iteration. Measured in tools/htp-lab against a float64 reference, for each 32-lane block:

    mode 0, the f32 chain      438.6 cycles   NMSE 2.7e-14
    mode 4, the packed band     29.0 cycles   NMSE 2.9e-07

15 times faster. GDN_CONV_CHUNK is the largest single op of a 512-token prefill of the 4B, at
27 % of the time on the digital signal processor, thus this is the largest prefill change of
the series. The op runs when a batch has more than one token, thus it serves the prefill and
the speculative verify, and not the single-token decode step.

The error

2.9e-07 of NMSE against a baseline of 2.7e-14. The consumer of this output, the chunked gated
delta net, already measures 3.0e-07 of its own, and the bound that the backend tests apply is
2e-06, thus this value costs nothing downstream. It is a regression from an exact baseline and
a reviewer must see it. GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 0 takes the old path back.
diff -urN a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:59:39.046281562 +0300
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:59:39.062841780 +0300
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@
 //   3  f16 taps, f16 accumulate, f16 SiLU. Every product goes back to f16 before the sum.
 //   4  the packed path: f16 taps, 32-bit accumulate, int16 SiLU, 4 token rows in each iteration.
 #ifndef GDN_CONV_F16_MODE
-#define GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 0
+#define GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 4
 #endif
 static int gdn_conv_f16_mode = GDN_CONV_F16_MODE;
 
